# Dockerfile Management Guide

This guide provides detailed instructions for effective modifications to the [Dockerfile](mdc:docker/Dockerfile), to ensure consistency, maintainability, and adherence to best practices.

---

## Best Practices
- Employ multi-stage builds for clear separation of build and runtime dependencies.
- Combine related `RUN` commands to reduce image layers.
- Always use `--no-cache` with `apk` for up-to-date packages.
- Explicit version number in `pecl install` to ensure PHP version compatibility.
- Ensure packages and extensions are installed, copied, or enabled in alphabetical order.
- Document all changes in [CHANGELOG.md](mdc:CHANGELOG.md)

---

## Adding Dependencies or PHP Extensions
- Add Alpine packages dependencies:  
  `RUN apk add --no-cache <package>`.
- Install PHP extensions:  
  `RUN pecl install <extension>` or `RUN docker-php-ext-install <extension>`.
- Copy `.so` files to the runtime stage as shown in the current Dockerfile.
- Enable extensions using `docker-php-ext-enable` command.

---

## Updating Base Versions

- Modify `ARG PHP_VERSION` at the top of the Dockerfile.
- Update `ARG` versions (e.g., `XDEBUG_VERSION`, `REDIS_VERSION`, `COMPOSER_VERSION`).
- Adjust in the [docker-compose.yml](mdc:docker-compose.yml) to reflect image `ARG` versions.

---

## Image Optimization
- Always use base images with alpine tag.
- Copy only essential files between build stages.
- Copy only essential local files into the Docker image.
- Clean up temporary files.

---

## Security
- Execute as non-root user `www-data`.
- Ensure correct permissions for directories and files.
- Avoid exposing sensitive data or credentials.

---

## Testing
- Ensure the image builds without errors.
- Confirm all required PHP extensions are enabled.
- Validate that composer are enabled.
- Check if the image starts with non-root user.
- Verify that the entrypoint (`supervisord`) starts correctly.

---

## Examples

### Adding PHP Extension

```dockerfile
# In the build stage
RUN pecl install <new-extension> \
    && docker-php-ext-enable <new-extension>
RUN PHP_EXT_DIR=$(php-config --extension-dir) \
    && cp ${PHP_EXT_DIR}/<new-extension>.so /tmp/php_extensions

# In the runtime stage
RUN PHP_EXT_DIR=$(php-config --extension-dir) \
    && cp /tmp/php_extensions/<new-extension>.so ${PHP_EXT_DIR}
RUN docker-php-ext-enable <new-extension>
```

